IMPORT prelude

-- Acts Interpretation Act 1954 (Qld), Part 4 -- References to Acts and other laws (ss 14E to 14J).
-- A reference rule says what a reference to a thing picks up; the thing referred to is described by plain yes or no inputs.

§ `Part 4 -- References`

§§ `s 14E -- References to Acts generally`

-- src:145 | An Act passed by Parliament, or any earlier legislature empowered to pass laws for Queensland, may be referred to by the word Act alone.
@ref s 14E (src:145-145)
GIVEN `the Act was passed by Parliament, or by an earlier legislature empowered to pass laws for Queensland` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Act may be referred to by the word Act alone (s 14E)` IS
    IF `the Act was passed by Parliament, or by an earlier legislature empowered to pass laws for Queensland` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

§§ `s 14F -- References to particular Acts`

DECLARE `Way of citing an Act` IS ONE OF
    `by its short title`
    `by reference to the year in which it was passed and its number`
    `in another way`

-- (1): an Act may be cited (a) by its short title or (b) by year and number.  A permission; another way is outside it: NOTHING.
-- FORK a way of citing that is neither (a) nor (b): NOTHING (the grant names two ways and does not say another is refused) || JUST FALSE
-- src:147 | (1) An Act may be cited—
-- src:148 | (a) by its short title; or
-- src:149 | (b) by reference to the year in which it was passed and its number.
@ref s 14F(1) (src:147-149)
GIVEN way IS A `Way of citing an Act`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `an Act may be cited in the way (s 14F(1))` IS
    CONSIDER way
    WHEN `in another way` THEN NOTHING
    OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- (2): a Commonwealth Act may be cited (a) by its short title or (b) in another way sufficient in a Commonwealth Act, together with a reference to the Commonwealth.
-- src:155 | (2) A Commonwealth Act may be cited—
-- src:156 | (a) by its short title; or
-- src:157 | (b) in another way sufficient in a Commonwealth Act for the citation of such an Act;
-- src:158 | together with a reference to the Commonwealth.
@ref s 14F(2) (src:155-158)
GIVEN `the citation is by its short title or in another way sufficient in a Commonwealth Act for the citation of such an Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the citation is together with a reference to the Commonwealth` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a Commonwealth Act may be cited in the way (s 14F(2))` IS
    IF `the citation is by its short title or in another way sufficient in a Commonwealth Act for the citation of such an Act` AND `the citation is together with a reference to the Commonwealth`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:159 | (3) An Act of another State or a Territory may be cited—
-- src:160 | (a) by its short title; or
-- src:161 | (b) in another way sufficient in an Act of the State or Territory for the citation of such an Act;
-- src:162 | together with a reference to the State or Territory.
@ref s 14F(3) (src:159-162)
GIVEN `the citation is by its short title or in another way sufficient in an Act of the State or Territory for the citation of such an Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the citation is together with a reference to the State or Territory` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `an Act of another State or a Territory may be cited in the way (s 14F(3))` IS
    IF `the citation is by its short title or in another way sufficient in an Act of the State or Territory for the citation of such an Act` AND `the citation is together with a reference to the State or Territory`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING

DECLARE `Reference to the United Kingdom` IS ONE OF
    `the United Kingdom`
    `the term UK`
    `the term Imperial Act`
    `the term Imp`
    `no such reference`

-- src:163 | (4) A British Act may be cited—
-- src:164 | (a) by its short title; or
-- src:165 | (b) in another way sufficient in a British Act for the citation of such an Act;
-- src:166 | together with a reference to the United Kingdom or the term ‘UK’, ‘Imperial Act’ or ‘Imp’.
@ref s 14F(4) (src:163-166)
GIVEN `the citation is by its short title or in another way sufficient in a British Act for the citation of such an Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      reference IS A `Reference to the United Kingdom`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a British Act may be cited in the way (s 14F(4))` IS
    CONSIDER reference
    WHEN `no such reference` THEN NOTHING
    OTHERWISE IF `the citation is by its short title or in another way sufficient in a British Act for the citation of such an Act` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

§§ `s 14G -- References to enactments`

-- src:168 | (1) An enactment may be cited by reference to the provision of the Act in which it is contained.
@ref s 14G(1) (src:168-168)
GIVEN `the enactment is contained in a provision of the Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `an enactment may be cited by reference to the provision of the Act in which it is contained (s 14G(1))` IS
    IF `the enactment is contained in a provision of the Act` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

DECLARE `Copy by which a reference to an enactment is made` IS ONE OF
    `an official copy of the Act`
    `an official copy of the Act as amended`
    `any other copy`

-- FORK a reference made according to a copy that is not an official copy: NOTHING (s 14G(2) names the copies and does not say what follows otherwise) || JUST FALSE
-- src:169 | (2) The reference is to be made according to an official copy of—
-- src:170 | (a) the Act; or
-- src:171 | (b) the Act as amended.
@ref s 14G(2) (src:169-171)
GIVEN copy IS A `Copy by which a reference to an enactment is made`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the reference is made according to a copy the section names (s 14G(2))` IS
    CONSIDER copy
    WHEN `any other copy` THEN NOTHING
    OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

DECLARE `Kind of Act` IS ONE OF
    `an Act of Queensland`
    `a Commonwealth Act`
    `an Act of another State`
    `a Territory Act`
    `a British Act`
    `anything else`

-- "Act includes Commonwealth Act, Act of another State, Territory Act or British Act."  "Includes" does not close the list.
-- src:172 | (3) In this section—
-- src:173 | Act includes Commonwealth Act, Act of another State, Territory Act or British Act.
@ref s 14G(3) (src:172-173)
GIVEN kind IS A `Kind of Act`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the kind is an Act in s 14G (s 14G(3), definition Act)` IS
    CONSIDER kind
    WHEN `anything else` THEN NOTHING
    OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- src:174 | enactment includes any portion of an Act.
@ref s 14G(3), definition enactment (src:174-174)
GIVEN `the thing is a portion of an Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the thing is an enactment in s 14G (s 14G(3), definition enactment)` IS
    IF `the thing is a portion of an Act` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

-- official copy (a): of an Act of Queensland or an Act of Queensland as amended -- "see schedule 1, definition official copy".
-- src:175 | official copy—
-- src:176 | (a) of an Act of Queensland or an Act of Queensland as amended—see schedule 1, definition official copy; or
@ref s 14G(3), definition official copy, paragraph (a) (src:175-176)
GIVEN `the copy is an official copy within schedule 1, definition official copy` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a copy of an Act of Queensland or of an Act of Queensland as amended is an official copy (s 14G(3), definition official copy, paragraph (a))` IS
    JUST `the copy is an official copy within schedule 1, definition official copy`

-- src:177 | (b) of an Act of another jurisdiction or an Act of another jurisdiction as amended—means a copy, including a reproduction in electronic form, of the Act or the Act as amended that, under a law of the jurisdiction, is presumed to be a correct copy of the Act or the Act as amended, in the absence of evidence to the contrary.
@ref s 14G(3), definition official copy, paragraph (b) (src:177-177)
GIVEN `under a law of the jurisdiction the copy is presumed to be a correct copy of the Act or the Act as amended, in the absence of evidence to the contrary` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a copy of an Act of another jurisdiction or of such an Act as amended is an official copy (s 14G(3), definition official copy, paragraph (b))` IS
    JUST `under a law of the jurisdiction the copy is presumed to be a correct copy of the Act or the Act as amended, in the absence of evidence to the contrary`

§§ `s 14H -- References taken to be included in reference to law`

DECLARE `Version of a law` IS ONE OF
    `the law as originally made`
    `the law as amended from time to time since it was originally made`
    `the law as remade`
    `the law as remade, and as amended from time to time since it was remade`
    `the other law as in force when the provision was remade`
    `the other law as in force when the provision was remade, and as amended from time to time since the provision was remade`
    `any other version`

-- (1): a reference to a law includes (a) as made and amended; (b) if repealed and remade since the reference was made, the law as remade and as amended;
-- (c) if a relevant provision was omitted and remade in another law since the reference was made, the other law as then in force, and as amended.  "Includes".
-- src:179 | (1) In an Act, a reference to a law (including the Act) includes a reference to the following—
-- src:180 | (a) the law as originally made, and as amended from time to time since it was originally made;
-- src:181 | (b) if the law has been repealed and remade (with or without modification) since the reference was made—the law as remade, and as amended from time to time since it was remade;
-- src:182 | (c) if a relevant provision of the law has been omitted and remade (with or without modification) in another law since the reference was made—the other law as in force when the provision was remade, and as amended from time to time since the provision was remade.
@ref s 14H(1) (src:179-182)
GIVEN version IS A `Version of a law`
      `the law has been repealed and remade (with or without modification) since the reference was made` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a relevant provision of the law has been omitted and remade (with or without modification) in another law since the reference was made` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a reference to a law includes a reference to the version (s 14H(1))` IS
    CONSIDER version
    WHEN `the law as originally made` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `the law as amended from time to time since it was originally made` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `the law as remade` THEN IF `the law has been repealed and remade (with or without modification) since the reference was made` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING
    WHEN `the law as remade, and as amended from time to time since it was remade` THEN IF `the law has been repealed and remade (with or without modification) since the reference was made` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING
    WHEN `the other law as in force when the provision was remade` THEN
        IF `a relevant provision of the law has been omitted and remade (with or without modification) in another law since the reference was made` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING
    WHEN `the other law as in force when the provision was remade, and as amended from time to time since the provision was remade` THEN
        IF `a relevant provision of the law has been omitted and remade (with or without modification) in another law since the reference was made` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING
    WHEN `any other version` THEN NOTHING

-- src:183 | (2) In an Act, a reference to a provision of a law (including the Act) includes a reference to the following—
-- src:184 | (a) the provision as originally made, and as amended from time to time since it was originally made;
-- src:185 | (b) if the provision has been omitted and remade (with or without modification and whether in the law or another law) since the reference was made—the provision as remade, and as amended from time to time since it was remade.
@ref s 14H(2) (src:183-185)
GIVEN version IS A `Version of a law`
      `the provision has been omitted and remade (with or without modification and whether in the law or another law) since the reference was made` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a reference to a provision of a law includes a reference to the version (s 14H(2))` IS
    CONSIDER version
    WHEN `the law as originally made` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `the law as amended from time to time since it was originally made` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `the law as remade` THEN IF `the provision has been omitted and remade (with or without modification and whether in the law or another law) since the reference was made` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING
    WHEN `the law as remade, and as amended from time to time since it was remade` THEN IF `the provision has been omitted and remade (with or without modification and whether in the law or another law) since the reference was made` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING
    OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- src:186 | (3) In this section—
-- src:187 | law includes a law of the Commonwealth, another State or a Territory.
@ref s 14H(3) (src:186-187)
GIVEN kind IS A `Kind of Act`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the kind is a law in s 14H (s 14H(3), definition law)` IS
    CONSIDER kind
    WHEN `a Commonwealth Act` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `an Act of another State` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `a Territory Act` THEN JUST TRUE
    OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- src:188 | make includes enact.
@ref s 14H(3), definition make (src:188-188)
GIVEN `the thing is to enact` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `make includes enact (s 14H(3), definition make)` IS
    IF `the thing is to enact` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

§§ `ss 14I and 14J -- changed short titles, repealed or expired laws`

-- src:190 | (1) If the short title or citation of a law is amended, a reference in an Act to the short title or citation includes a reference to the short title or citation as amended.
@ref s 14I(1) (src:190-190)
GIVEN `the short title or citation of the law is amended` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a reference in an Act to the short title or citation includes a reference to the short title or citation as amended (s 14I(1))` IS
    IF `the short title or citation of the law is amended` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

-- src:191 | (2) In this section—
-- src:192 | law includes a law of the Commonwealth, another State or a Territory.
@ref s 14I(2) (src:191-192)
GIVEN kind IS A `Kind of Act`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the kind is a law in s 14I (s 14I(2), definition law)` IS
    CONSIDER kind
    WHEN `a Commonwealth Act` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `an Act of another State` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `a Territory Act` THEN JUST TRUE
    OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- s 14J(1): if an Act refers to another law as repealed or expired, the reference is to the other law as in force immediately before it was repealed or expired.
DECLARE `State of a law that a reference to a repealed or expired law is to` IS ONE OF
    `the other law as in force immediately before it was repealed or expired`
    `the other law as in force at some other time`

-- src:194 | (1) If an Act refers to another law as repealed or expired, the reference is to the other law as in force immediately before it was repealed or expired.
-- src:195 | Example—
-- src:196 | The ‘repealed ABC Act 1950’ is a reference to the ABC Act 1950 as in force immediately before it was repealed.
@ref s 14J(1) (src:194-196)
GIVEN `the Act refers to another law as repealed or expired` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE `State of a law that a reference to a repealed or expired law is to`
DECIDE `the state of the other law to which a reference to a repealed or expired law is (s 14J(1))` IS
    IF `the Act refers to another law as repealed or expired`
    THEN JUST `the other law as in force immediately before it was repealed or expired`
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:197 | (2) In this section—
-- src:198 | law includes a law of the Commonwealth, another State or a Territory.
@ref s 14J(2) (src:197-198)
GIVEN kind IS A `Kind of Act`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the kind is a law in s 14J (s 14J(2), definition law)` IS
    CONSIDER kind
    WHEN `a Commonwealth Act` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `an Act of another State` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `a Territory Act` THEN JUST TRUE
    OTHERWISE NOTHING
